### What is Agentic Document?
An Agentic Document refers to a document that is dynamically managed, processed, or utilized by AI agents within an agentic workflow. These workflows leverage advanced AI systems capable of reasoning, decision-making, and executing tasks autonomously.
The candidates include documents regarding onboarding processes, reclamation policies, and documentation of internal, technical knowledge for manufacturing or troubleshooting. 

![How does Operational Document work?](../../assets/CleverFlow-HowItWorks.png)

### When do we need Agentic Documents?
Link different types of documents and data sources to create a unified view of information.
Automate the processing of documents to reduce manual effort and errors.
Turn static documents into interactive and dynamic content.
Extract key data from unstructured or semi-structured content.
Analyze and interpret information to answer complex queries or generate insights.
Adapt workflows based on real-time changes in data or user requirements

### Why is it important to automate Operational Documents?
Automation enables a Single Place of Truth for both documentation and its use:
- Content writers can visualize and test the logic of their documents at the time of composition.
- Supporters can visually find and prove the answer to an input query with the given documents in their daily business.
- Technicians can integrate ad hoc Agentic Solutions into these documents to enable interactivity and automatic processing.

### Who are we?
CLEVER°FLOW plays a central role in documenting and reasoning Technical and Support Documents within our [CLEVER°NOW Eco-System](https://clevernow.com).

### What are Core Concepts?

{% cardgrid %}
{% card title="Interactive Content with Markdoc" icon="seti:markdown" %}
Markdown `.md` and the interactive flavor Markdoc `.mdoc` (invented by Stripe) are used to create documents.

[Read more](/docs/interactive-content) 
{% /card %}

{% card title="Simple Logics with Behaviour Tree" icon="seti:puppet" %}
Behaviour Trees are visually used to define the logic required in the documents.
{% /card %}

{% card title="Scalabilty and Observability with Event-Sourcing" icon="seti:vite" %}
Inference process is persisted as a sequence of events, which can be replayed to recreate the state of the system at any point in time.
{% /card %}

{% card title="Integration with Agentic AI Frameworks" icon="seti:bicep" %}
Easily integrate with your favorite Agentic AI Frameworks such as LangGraph, Microsoft AutoGen, etc
{% /card %}

{% card title="Pluggability with Web Components" icon="seti:webpack" %}
Easily plug in any Website to create a rich user experience.
{% /card %}
{% /cardgrid %}